        "noSubjects": "No obstacles yet.",
        "gmNotes": "<p><strong>Example: Chase, Chase Down.</strong> The PCs pursue. Built for four level-1 PCs: base DC 15, easy 13. Six obstacles, a short chase.</p><p>A pickpocket has the party's letter of introduction and bolts through the market. Rounds are about a minute. The pickpocket acts first; the PCs act second.</p><p><strong>Each roll:</strong> a success earns 1 Chase Point, a critical success 2, and a critical failure loses 1. Use + and − on the obstacle. When it is full, mark it Complete, add 1 to Party and reveal the next obstacle. Chase Points don't carry over.</p><p><strong>The pickpocket</strong> starts one obstacle ahead and moves 1 each round on Next round.</p><p><strong>It ends</strong> when Party reaches the Pickpocket's obstacle (they're caught: run the scene), or the Pickpocket gets past obstacle 6 into the sewers.</p>",
